mayor Carolyn Goodman unveiling a new  sculpture today in the Las Vegas  storytelling Garden the sculpture honors  those lost on one October it is called  flight of healing it stands about 10  feet tall the sculpture's central tree  trunk embodies strength and the  butterflies represent healing and a  Guiding Light  I want to thank the designers of this  sculpture who are themselves survivors  of that painful night  the project was funded through the  mayor's fund for Las Vegas life to  support key City initiatives the entire  project cost about thirty nine thousand  dollars
 

